  "slug": "perturbation-profiling-e9d8",
  "summary": "Six preprints pair perturbation or differentiation with chromatin readouts, extending resolution from hub dynamics to single molecules and spatial context.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is resolving how regulatory state responds to perturbation or cell-state change using chromatin-level readouts. Methodological advances include Perturb-Tags, which pairs spatially barcoded CRISPR perturbations with single-nucleus expression and accessibility to expose non-autonomous effects; MolMap, which maps compound-specific accessibility changes to unmodified small molecules in non-crosslinked nuclei; and ChIMe-seq, which jointly profiles histone modifications, DNA methylation and nucleosome positioning in single molecules. Mechanistic studies add temporal and structural dimensions: a Mastermind-to-Broad hub handover sustains hindsight transcription after Notch activation, super-enhancers rewire extensively across three differentiation systems, and genome folding variability differs between pluripotent and hepatocyte-like cells, linked to nuclear position and gene expression variability.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
}
